  "editorial_note": "GitHub listed twelve projects this Wednesday morning, and eight of them were featured here in the past week. Today's three picks are all first appearances: Addy Osmani's ==engineering skills pack for AI coding agents==, Topcoat, ==an early full-stack Rust web framework from the Tokio project==, and Sure, the community-run personal finance app. Curation order reflects practical interest, not GitHub rank. Trending is not a release date or an endorsement.",
  "coverage_notes": [
    "GitHub's daily listing held only 12 rows at capture, short against the 13 to 18 rows of early November but in line with the 9 and 11 rows of the last two days. The raw page was checked: it contains exactly twelve listing rows, so the short list is GitHub's.",
    "All 12 listing entries were inspected. Exact public GitHub API metadata and recent releases were checked at about 07:01:30 UTC for every entry; README files of the three picks were read at about 07:02 UTC. Every checked repository was active and unarchived.",
    "Eight entries featured in the past seven days were left out without a new primary-sourced reason: meta/astryx, sherlock-project/sherlock and ranxianglei/billion-context (8 November), anthropics/skills, anthropics/claude-quickstarts and google-deepmind/mujoco (9 November), and homeassistant-ai/ha-mcp and vercel-labs/agent-browser (10 November).",
    "meta/astryx shipped v0.7.12 and v0.7.13 on 10 November; their notes describe component polish and fixes (sheets, chat composer, lightbox gestures, accessibility), which we did not judge a material change since the 8 November pick.",
    "mattpocock/skills was featured on 31 October; its latest release, v1.3.2, predates that pick, so it was left out.",
    "The preceding seven calendar dates, 4-10 November, were checked for local history; all seven editions exist.",
    "The official listing was captured at 08:01:16 Europe/Paris. Literal stars-today labels are GitHub's displayed period figures; API total stars and README evidence were checked separately at the times shown per card. They are not an independently audited rolling 24-hour growth measurement.",
    "Feature descriptions come from each project's own README and release notes and are the maintainers' claims. No candidate code, installer, binary, plugin, skill or model was installed, downloaded or run, and none of this is a security audit or endorsement."
  ],
