      "readme_source_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/addyosmani/agent-skills/readme",
      "evidence_urls": [
        "https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills",
        "https://api.github.com/repos/addyosmani/agent-skills",
        "https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills/releases/tag/0.6.15"
      ],
      "description": "Agent Skills is ==a pack of 25 plain-Markdown engineering skills for AI coding agents==, written by Addy Osmani. Nine slash commands follow a spec, plan, build, test, review and ship lifecycle, and the README gives install paths for Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, Gemini CLI, Copilot and other hosts.",
      "why_interesting": "First time on our list. Rather than prompts, it packages ==senior-engineer habits as enforceable steps==: spec before code, small test-driven tasks, a five-axis review before merge. Release 0.6.15 (31 October) stopped its staged-secret check from printing the secrets it finds and made the security and accessibility gates actually fail CI.",
      "caveat": "Skills and hooks steer an agent that can edit code and run commands, so ==read what you install==; 0.6.15 itself fixed a check that leaked secrets into transcripts and a hook that could corrupt protected code. A per-skill install omits the shared reference checklists, and the README's /build auto mode runs every task after one plan approval, pausing only on failures or risky steps. We did not install it."
    },
    {
      "repository": "tokio-rs/topcoat",
      "url": "https://github.com/tokio-rs/topcoat",
      "trending_rank": 10,
      "category": "Developer tools / web framework",
      "language": "Rust",
      "license": "MIT",
      "stars_total": 6962,
      "stars_period": 192,
      "stars_period_label": "192 stars today",
      "archived": false,
      "metadata_checked_at": "2026-11-11T07:01:32Z",
      "readme_checked_at": "2026-11-11T07:01:56Z",
      "readme_source_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/tokio-rs/topcoat/readme",
      "evidence_urls": [
        "https://github.com/tokio-rs/topcoat",
        "https://api.github.com/repos/tokio-rs/topcoat",
        "https://github.com/tokio-rs/topcoat/releases/tag/v0.12.0",
        "https://github.com/tokio-rs/topcoat/releases/tag/v0.12.1"
      ],
      "description": "Topcoat is ==a batteries-included full-stack web framework for Rust== from the Tokio organisation. Pages and components are async Rust functions rendered on the server, with an HTML-like view! macro, module-based routing, an asset bundler, Tailwind support and an editable component library copied into your project.",
      "why_interesting": "First time on our list. Its distinctive trick: ==a $(...) expression is type-checked Rust that also runs as JavaScript== in the browser, so small interactions need no server round trip, no WebAssembly bundle and no client build step. v0.12.0 (9 November) unified its context model and v0.12.1 (10 November) added OpenAPI generation.",
      "caveat": "The README says it is ==early-stage and experimental; expect breaking changes==, and v0.12.0's own notes say most apps need many small edits to upgrade. Static export, validations and more reactivity are still roadmap items, so it is a framework to evaluate rather than to bet production on yet. We did not install it."
    },
