      "evidence_urls": [
        "https://github.com/we-promise/sure",
        "https://api.github.com/repos/we-promise/sure",
        "https://github.com/we-promise/sure/releases/tag/v0.7.6",
        "https://github.com/we-promise/sure/releases/tag/v2026.11.10-alpha"
      ],
      "description": "Sure is ==a self-hostable personal finance and net-worth app==, a community fork of the abandoned Maybe Finance project. It is a Ruby app that self-hosts with Docker alongside PostgreSQL and Redis, and the README lists a browser, a macOS desktop app, a mobile app, API clients and LLM agents as ways in.",
      "why_interesting": "First time on our list. It is ==a rescued codebase with active community upkeep==: Maybe's team stopped in 2023 after, by their account, nearly a million dollars of work, and Sure keeps shipping. The 10 November nightly added a Monarch importer, account statements in the API and a fix that refuses another family's categories in the API.",
      "caveat": "You hold your own financial data, so ==backups, updates and access control are on you==. The optional AI features need an OpenAI token or an external assistant, which then receives the questions and data you send it. Nightly tags are alpha builds with debug mobile apps, the latest stable is v0.7.6 (31 October), and AGPL-3.0 applies to anyone serving a modified version. We did not install it."
    }
